\b\fs28 Algorithm to search an element in Binary search tree\par
\b0\fs24 Search (root, item)  \par
Step 1 - if (item = root \f1\u8594?\f0  data) or (root = NULL)  \par
return root  \par
else if (item < root \f1\u8594?\f0  data)  \par
return Search(root \f1\u8594?\f0  left, item)  \par
else  \par
return Search(root \f1\u8594?\f0  right, item)  \par
END if  \par
Step 2 - END  \par
\b\fs28 Algorithm\f2  \f0 for\f2  \f0 Insertion\f2  \f0 in\f2  \f0 a\f2  \f0 Binary\f2  \f0 Search\f2  \f0 Tree\f2  (\f0 BST\f2 )\f0\par
\b0\fs24 A\f2  \f0 Binary\f2  \f0 Search\f2  \f0 Tree\f2  (\f0 BST\f2 ) \f0 follows\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 property\f2  \f0 that\f2 :\f0\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qj The\f2  \f0 left\f2  \f0 subtree\f2  \f0 contains\f2  \f0 nodes\f2  \f0 with\f2  \f0 values\f2  \f0 less\f2  \f0 than\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 root\f2 .\f0\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}The\f2  \f0 right\f2  \f0 subtree\f2  \f0 contains\f2  \f0 nodes\f2  \f0 with\f2  \f0 values\f2  \f0 greater\f2  \f0 than\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 root\f2 .\f0\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}Both\f2  \f0 left\f2  \f0 and\f2  \f0 right\f2  \f0 subtrees\f2  \f0 must\f2  \f0 also\f2  \f0 be\f2  \f0 BSTs\f2 .\f0\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qj\b Algorithm\f2  \f0 for\f2  \f0 Insertion\f2  \f0 in\f2  \f0 BST\f2 :\f0\par
Step 1:\b0  If\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 root\f2  \f0 is\f2  \f0 NULL\f2 , \f0 create\f2  \f0 a\f2  \f0 new\f2  \f0 node\f2  \f0 and\f2  \f0 return\f2  \f0 it\f2  \f0 as\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 root\f2 .\f0\par
\b Step 2:\b0  Compare\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 value\f2  \f0 to\f2  \f0 be\f2  \f0 inserted\f2  \f0 with\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 root\rquote s\f2  \f0 value\f2 :\f0\par
\tab If\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 value\f2  \f0 is\f2  \f0 less\f2  \f0 than\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 root\f2 , \f0 recursively\f2  \f0 insert\f2  \f0 it\f2  \f0 in\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 left\f2  \f0 subtree\f2 .\f0\par
\tab If\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 value\f2  \f0 is\f2  \f0 greater\f2  \f0 than\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 root\f2 , \f0 recursively\f2  \f0 insert\f2  \f0 it\f2  \f0 in\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 right\f2  \f0 subtree\f2 .\f0\par
\b Step 3:\b0  Once\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 correct\f2  \f0 position\f2  \f0 is\f2  \f0 found\f2 , \f0 insert\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 new\f2  \f0 node\f2  \f0 as\f2  \f0 a\f2  \f0 leaf\f2 .\f0\par
\b Step 4:\b0  Return\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 modified\f2  \f0 tree\f2  \f0 with\f2  \f0 the\f2  \f0 newly\f2  \f0 inserted\f2  \f0 node\f2 .\par
\b\f0\fs28 Pseudocode for Insertion in BST\par
\b0\fs24 Function Insert(Node root, int key):\par
    If root is NULL:\par
        return CreateNewNode(key)\par
\par
    If key < root->value:\par
        root->left = Insert(root.left, key)\par
    Else if key > root.value:\par
        root.right = Insert(root.right, key)\par
    Return root\par
\b\fs28 Deletion in Binary Search tree\par
\b0\fs24 In a binary search tree, we must delete a node from the tree by keeping in mind that the property of BST is not violated. To delete a node from BST, there are three possible situations occur:\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qj The node to be deleted is the leaf node, or,\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}The node to be deleted has only one child, and,\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}The node to be deleted has two children\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qj We will understand the situations listed above in detail.\par
\par
\b\fs28\lang9 When the node to be deleted is the leaf node\b0\fs24\par
It is the simplest case to delete a node in BST. Here, we have to replace the leaf node with NULL and simply free the allocated space.\par
